{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/archive/component/aspace_be02a7be85c983004a03381ead6c699d","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"aspace_be02a7be85c983004a03381ead6c699d","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"accession number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355"}],"content":"1.1.2","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Photographs","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Access restriction statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/accessrestrict"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eSome materials fragile. May require handling by the Archivist.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Legal status statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/userestrict"}],"content":null,"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Scope and Content statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/scopecontent"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eThe Chabot family photographs sub-series includes, but is not limited to the following materials: 173 photographs and slides of Maria Chabot alone and with family, friends and pets from her infancy to old age. The last dated photograph is 1994. Also, a poem by Mary Van Derlip Chabot about M.C. as a baby and a chromolithographic print with a poem about motherhood, which was found in back of a framed baby picture of M.C. 70 photographs, slides, and negatives of Olive Anderson Johnson Chabot, M.C.'s mother, alone and with family, friends and pets from childhood to old age. The last dated picture is August 1973. 25 photographs of M.C.'s half-brothers and half-sister. 2 photographs of Frederick C. Chabot, 3 photographs of Edith Chabot Kilburn and a boyfriend, and 20 photographs of J.K. Johnston. 1 photograph of Glenn Anderson, O.J.C.'s brother.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Related Material","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/relatedmaterial"}],"content":[],"type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"Set"}